hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to an  edition of ask Evan today's episode is  brought to you by Telus talks business  have got a great face book page call  telus off business he could check out  and lots of resources and ideas for  canadian entrepreneurs today's question  comes from one of our pulse ox business  readers who is asking about do you need  a college or university education to be  able to two of the B's a successful  entrepreneur so the question came in  saying hi Evan this article's very  inspiring what always puzzles me though  about most of these success stories is  that most of them didn't finish their  college education is that they're  smarter than most people or is that they  were just really convinced that college  wouldn't help them with their with their  business someone please answer this for  me so thank you for the question that's  a really tough one I think the college  dropouts are more well-known it's a  bigger story I guess because they take  the road less traveled I think if you  look at most successful entrepreneurs  today most modern day successful  entrepreneurs you'll find that they did  go to college and university they could  be putting yourself at a disadvantage if  you didn't at least go and get your  undergraduate degree you get to meet new  people and just in case you have a  fallback plan you will get a job if the  business doesn't work out so if you  think if you look at the most successful  entrepreneurs now you'll find that most  of them did go to college or university  if you look at the previous successful  entrepreneurs you know the ones from the  past I think you'll find two things one  some of them may not have gone to  college university it wasn't for lack of  desire it was for usually a lack of  resources so they didn't have the money  to go or they were they might have  started and they needed to drop out  because they didn't have enough money so  they had to start something that just to  try to sustain themselves so that's  that's that's very common is that in  four previous entrepreneurs successful  entrepreneurs in history they may have  started but you know they didn't have  the ability to continue or even get  started because they didn't have the  money to do it it's not that they didn't  want to do it though and if you look at  a lot of those successful entrepreneurs  you'll also find that at the beginning  it really made them doubt themselves  because they didn't feel good enough  they felt inadequate they felt they  weren't as educators of the people and  they felt that that actually held them  back with the business so you'll find  the rare exception you'll find some  people who say you know college  university wasn't really helpful and I  didn't want to do that in want to launch  my own business instead but for the most  part you'll find that people either went  to college university or they wanted to  go but weren't able to so you won't find  many people will say don't go to college  university in my own experience I went  to university what university of toronto  and did my undergrad degree there and  that was a turning point for me so a lot  of my friends were going off to do jobs  i'd already started my business  part-time while i was in university and  i had the option to go and work at some  big companies and i thought you're on  i'm taking a year off and instead of  going to get a job I'm gonna go do my  own business and it was something I felt  I'm I might regret and a lot of times  you start a job and then you start  working on your career path and the  excitement about said in the business  starts to fade and then there's it's too  much of a risk to do because you have a  safe secure job wherever you do it right  at the beginning I felt a lot of those  opportunities would still be there for  me I could always go back and get those  jobs if after the one year didn't work  out so I did finish my university  education in terms of the undergrad  degree for the four years and then I  started off doing one year of doing my  own business full time and then never  went back to go get a job so it ended up  working out for me but I would always  recommend going to college university if  you can try to take courses that you  think will help you with your career and  also you know learn about  entrepreneurship if there's any kind of  entrepreneurship stream that you can  learn from try to get involved in the  different programs that they have if  there's anything that supports start up  and you kind of start up club or  investor club get involved in that and  also try to meet people who are  entrepreneurs I think one of the  greatest experience you can get and long  lasting from a college university  education is being able to meet  interesting people who can hopefully  become lifelong friends and also  potential business partners for you for  future ventures so hopefully I'll help I  know a lot of people think about that  decision should i go to college universe  or not that's my take on it at least in  terms of my experience and what famous  entrepreneurs have gone through so  thanks for the question for those of you  watching if you liked the video please  give it a thumbs up I'd also love to  hear all you have to think if you want  to leave a comment under the video or if  you have another question as well I  always read the common to come into and  I always appreciate those as well as the  the thumbs up the commensal thank you  and also don't forget to check out the  Telus talks business Facebook page they  were kind enough to sponsor this video  so thank you and a lot of great  resources there so thank you and we'll  see you in the next episode  you
 

